"The first operational tension lies in 'governing inside information and selective leaks during confidential M&A negotiations'. Under European Market Abuse Regulation ('MAR') and equivalent securities statutes, exploratory merger or joint-venture negotiations may lawfully be kept confidential only so long as strict technical conditions are met—including maintaining an up-to-date 'Insider List', enforcing cryptographic clean-room data access, and ensuring zero leakage. The instant specific transaction terms leak to financial media, causing unusual share-price movements, the legal justification for delayed disclosure evaporates instantaneously, compelling an immediate public announcement regardless of whether deal terms are finalised.",
