"To re-engineer Pan-European Specialty Paper & Packaging's cost architecture for structural resilience across future macroeconomic cycles, this note recommends four binding operational reforms: first, reducing the group's fixed-cost ratio from 68 % to below 52 % over thirty months through modular energy contracting, flexible shift-scheduling agreements, and shared-service automation; second, mandating automatic energy, pulp, and freight indexation clauses in all customer contracts exceeding six months; third, replacing incremental historical budgeting with an annual 'Zero-Based Overhead & SG&A Review' targeting €45 million in structural administrative savings; and fourth, ring-fencing continuous process-efficiency and energy-recovery capex from cyclical budget freezes.",
