"To govern currency volatility strategically across Meridian-Precision Optical & Medical Devices, this note recommends four integrated financial and industrial actions: first, establishing a 'Multi-Currency Supply-Chain Rebalancing Target' requiring at least 45 % of non-European component procurement and software engineering to be denominated in US dollars and Asian currencies within thirty-six months; second, deploying selective 'modular final-assembly postponement' in North America and Asia to match local revenue currencies without duplicating core optical-core manufacturing; third, matching foreign-subsidiary net asset exposures with local-currency debt issuance ('net-investment hedging'); and fourth, separating 'constant-currency operational performance' from foreign-exchange translation effects in executive bonus scorecards.",
