"The structural challenge confronting modern enterprises lies in 'normative proliferation and cross-jurisdictional taxonomy divergence'. Rather than converging onto a single global rulebook, international standard-setting bodies, regional legislators, and sectoral regulators have constructed dense, partially overlapping normative ecosystems that define identical concepts—such as 'material risk', 'critical third-party ICT provider', or 'Scope 3 supply-chain accountability'—with subtle legal variations, distinct audit frequencies, and incompatible reporting formats.",
