"Empirical studies of premier global compliance architectures demonstrate that mastering standard proliferation requires shifting from 'reactive rule-by-rule siloing' to 'integrated, controls-once-comply-many regulatory engineering'. By mapping overlapping international statutes onto a unified 'Enterprise Control Taxonomy', automating continuous control verification directly inside core IT and ERP workflows, and embedding risk-weighted assurance around genuine catastrophic hazards, leading enterprises cut compliance overhead while strengthening substantive integrity.",
