"To transform regulatory compliance at Helvetia-Meridian from a costly bureaucratic burden into an agile institutional capability, this note recommends four structural reforms: first, deploying a unified 'Integrated Control & Assurance Framework' mapping all EU, US, and international standards onto a single rationalised set of core controls ('test once, report many'); second, transitioning from annual manual self-attestations to automated 'Continuous Control Monitoring ('CCM')' embedded within enterprise data systems; third, establishing a cross-functional 'Regulatory Horizon-Scanning & Impact Council' assessing draft standards twelve to twenty-four months prior to enforcement; and fourth, shifting compliance KPIs from checklist completion rates to substantive risk-reduction outcomes.",
