      "However, fundraising valuations frequently suffer severe distortion when founders and late-stage investors rely on 'vanity intangible metrics and unverified exclusivity claims'. Counting raw unexamined patent filings without analysing claim breadth, overlooking open-source licensing contamination ('copyleft viral obligations'), ignoring third-party training-data copyright encumbrances, or extrapolating pilot-customer proof-of-concept revenues as permanent recurring software subscriptions systematically inflates valuations beyond sustainable economic fundamentals.",
