"Furthermore, poorly sequenced 'unilateral raw-export bans' without domestic processing capacity or regional value-chain coordination can inadvertently backfire—triggering informal smuggling across porous borders, deterring upstream exploration capital, and stranding raw harvests when domestic refineries lack working capital or reliable grid power to absorb output.",
