      "To transform commercial SOEs into self-financing, high-performing engines of economic development, this note recommends four binding governance reforms: first, transferring state shareholdings out of line ministries into an independent, professionally staffed 'Central Sovereign Ownership & Portfolio Agency' governed by strict commercial performance compacts; second, appointing merit-selected, predominantly independent boards of directors with full authority over CEO recruitment and executive remuneration; third, codifying and explicitly funding all non-commercial 'Public Service Obligations ('PSOs')' directly through transparent annual parliamentary budget appropriations; and fourth, subjecting all major commercial SOEs to IFRS external audits, credit ratings, and selective minority stock-exchange listings.",
